---
// The Compose services and the calls between them, coloured by the documentation theme.
---

<figure class="diagram not-content">
  <div class="diagram-scroll">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
      <title id="architecture-title">
        The browser calls nginx, which serves the React app and proxies /api to the Spring API. The
        API stores state in PostgreSQL and model files in MinIO, sends artifacts and inputs to the
        Python runtime, and reads Docker Compose through the operations agent.
      </title>
      <defs>
        <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto">
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="arrow-head"></path>
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <rect x="20" y="130" width="120" height="64" rx="10" class="box-subtle"></rect>
      <text x="80" y="158" text-anchor="middle" class="title">Browser</text>
      <text x="80" y="178" text-anchor="middle" class="small">people, software</text>

      <rect x="190" y="130" width="140" height="64" rx="10" class="box"></rect>
      <text x="260" y="158" text-anchor="middle" class="title">frontend</text>
      <text x="260" y="178" text-anchor="middle" class="small">nginx · React</text>

      <rect x="390" y="130" width="150" height="64" rx="10" class="box-accent"></rect>
      <text x="465" y="158" text-anchor="middle" class="title">spring-app</text>
      <text x="465" y="178" text-anchor="middle" class="small">auth · permissions · state</text>

      <rect x="600" y="130" width="140" height="64" rx="10" class="box"></rect>
      <text x="670" y="158" text-anchor="middle" class="title">py-analyzer</text>
      <text x="670" y="178" text-anchor="middle" class="small">load · predict · explain</text>

      <rect x="330" y="250" width="120" height="56" rx="10" class="box-subtle"></rect>
      <text x="390" y="275" text-anchor="middle" class="title">postgres</text>
      <text x="390" y="293" text-anchor="middle" class="small">application state</text>

      <rect x="480" y="250" width="120" height="56" rx="10" class="box-subtle"></rect>
      <text x="540" y="275" text-anchor="middle" class="title">minio</text>
      <text x="540" y="293" text-anchor="middle" class="small">model files</text>

      <rect x="405" y="24" width="120" height="56" rx="10" class="box-subtle"></rect>
      <text x="465" y="49" text-anchor="middle" class="title">ops-agent</text>
      <text x="465" y="67" text-anchor="middle" class="small">Docker Compose</text>

      <line x1="140" y1="162" x2="186" y2="162" class="edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
      <text x="163" y="152" text-anchor="middle" class="mono-muted">HTTPS</text>
      <line x1="330" y1="162" x2="386" y2="162" class="edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
      <text x="358" y="152" text-anchor="middle" class="mono-muted">/api</text>
      <line x1="540" y1="162" x2="596" y2="162" class="edge-accent" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
      <text x="568" y="152" text-anchor="middle" class="mono-muted">HTTP</text>
      <line x1="430" y1="194" x2="400" y2="246" class="edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
      <line x1="500" y1="194" x2="530" y2="246" class="edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
      <line x1="465" y1="130" x2="465" y2="84" class="edge-dashed" marker-end="url(#arrow)"></line>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>The Compose services. Only <code>frontend</code> (and PostgreSQL's port) is published on the host.</figcaption>
</figure>
